Database migrations (Alembic)
=============================

The database schema is owned by Alembic. `app/main.py` does NOT create tables —
if the schema is missing or stale, the app fails rather than silently diverging
from the migration history.

Run every command from the `backend/` directory.

Create or update a database
---------------------------
    ./venv/Scripts/alembic upgrade head

`python -m app.seed.seed` runs this for you before seeding, so a fresh clone
only needs the seed command.

After changing a model
----------------------
1. Edit the model under `app/models/`.
2. Generate the migration:

       ./venv/Scripts/alembic revision --autogenerate -m "short description"

3. READ the generated file in `alembic/versions/`. Autogenerate is a starting
   point, not an oracle — it does not detect renames (it emits a drop plus an
   add, which loses the data) and it cannot infer data backfills.
4. Apply it:

       ./venv/Scripts/alembic upgrade head

Useful commands
---------------
    alembic current              # which revision this database is on
    alembic history --verbose    # full revision history
    alembic downgrade -1         # undo the last migration

SQLite specifics
----------------
`env.py` sets `render_as_batch=True` for SQLite. SQLite cannot ALTER most
columns in place, so batch mode rebuilds the table (create new, copy rows, drop
old, rename) — this preserves existing data. Without it, most column changes
would fail outright on SQLite.

The database URL comes from `app.core.config.settings.DATABASE_URL`, not from
`alembic.ini`, so migrations always target the same database the app uses.
Override it with the `DATABASE_URL` environment variable when needed.

Adopting an existing database
-----------------------------
If you have a database that predates migrations and already matches the current
models, mark it as up to date instead of re-running the baseline:

    ./venv/Scripts/alembic stamp head
